[center][size=5][b][color=#ffd966]Date Time and Counter[/color][/b][/size][/center]

Adds an optional in-game clock alongside the day counter, using the game's own HUD style and clock data.

[b]Features[/b]
[list]
[*][color=#d9ead3]Show the current in-game day, the in-game time, or both.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#b6d7a8]Choose 12-hour or 24-hour time.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#6aa84f]Choose how often displayed minutes advance: every 1, 5, 10, 15, 30, or 60 in-game minutes.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]Attach the display below the location label, or detach it and position it independently.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#93c47d]When detached, optionally show a location-style HUD background and adjust the position and text size.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#6aa84f]Reposition the detached display by dragging it with the left mouse button. Press [b]Esc[/b] or right-click to finish and return to the Mods settings.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#b6d7a8]The display follows HUD visibility and hides during cinematics and when returning to the main menu.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#6aa84f]Uses the active game font and supports the game's available languages. Missing translations fall back to English.[/color][/*]
[/list]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.x[/url] - Tested with 5.4.23.5[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] 0.1.12 or newer.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Installation[/b]
Install the archive into the game's BepInEx folder, keeping the included folder structure. The plugin should be located at:
[code]BepInEx/plugins/GK2.DayCounter/GK2.DayCounter.dll[/code]

[b]Configuration[/b]
Open [b]Mods → Date Time and Counter → Settings[/b]. The day counter and clock can be enabled independently. When the display is attached to the location label, its position follows that label; independent positioning is available only while detached.

[b]Notes[/b]
The mod reads the game's in-game clock, so the displayed time follows game-time changes rather than the computer's real-world clock. It does not modify save files.
